  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nA westward drifting upper-level ridge will elongate over South \nCentral Texas Thursday before an upper low in the Gulf and a \ntrough to the west eventually force this feature south of the area\nlate this weekend. With southerly flow at the surface, increased \nmoisture continues over the area this week most notably Thursday \nand and Thursday night as a surge of higher PWAT values moves \ninland over South Central Texas. While rain chances extend over \nmuch of the area during this time, we are not expecting widespread\nshower and thunderstorm activity as the upper ridge continues to \ninfluence the area. Upper ridging looks to linger over the area \nthrough much of the weekend keep rain chances either out of the \narea or low during this time. Towards the very end of the forecast\nperiod, a series of shortwaves could impact Texas and could bring\nsome additional rain chances and possibly a slight decrease in \ntemperatures, but details remain uncertain.",
